WEBVTT

1
00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:15.849
Sophie Bulloch: Hi, Angie, sorry it took me a few minutes to be able to speak.

2
00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:17.950
Sophie Bulloch: Or anything.

3
00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:25.090
Sophie Bulloch: Hope you're okay. And for anyone listening in, this is…

4
00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:28.539
Sophie Bulloch: the Python SDK Office Hour, it's held…

5
00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:34.149
Sophie Bulloch: every two weeks at, 5pm UTC.

6
00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:39.960
Sophie Bulloch: And you can drop in when you want. It's available for, like, the full hour.

7
00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:43.249
Sophie Bulloch: And you can ask any questions.

8
00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:47.050
Sophie Bulloch: Regarding the Python SDK, so any open issues…

9
00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:50.489
Sophie Bulloch: That you are working on, you need some guidance.

10
00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:52.639
Sophie Bulloch: Or anything like that.

11
00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:58.469
Sophie Bulloch: Or maybe even if you're using the Python SDK, you can just drop in and ask any questions.

12
00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:07.829
Sophie Bulloch: Other than that, we will be kind of working in the background, so it's just a, I guess, like, a quiet meeting, but we are here.

13
00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:11.029
Sophie Bulloch: There's usually… usually at least one of us here.

14
00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:20.289
Sophie Bulloch: that will be able to answer a lot of the questions, and if not, we will, yeah, resolve it with… through Discord or something.

15
00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:22.960
Sophie Bulloch: So everybody is welcome here.

16
00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.019
Sophie Bulloch: Even if you are new to the Python SDK.

